  "_about": "CARNOTAURUS SASTREI (sculpt overlay, 2026-11-05, after the holotype skeletal, Hartman-style): 7.8 m nose to tail, the hips 2.1 m up, the body level over long slender legs (femur 1.03 m); a deep chest, a long tail broad at its root (the caudal ribs' caudofemoralis); a nearly straight, wide neck; a 0.6 m skull short, deep and boxy with a shallow upturned jaw and two thick conical horns over the eyes pointing out and up; absurdly small arms (the forearm a quarter of the humerus, the hand a stub). Rows of big feature scales along neck, back, flanks and tail (coat pattern `osteoderms`). Muted rust-brown back, grey-tan flanks, a pale belly. (2026-11-08) The HORNS are the engine's sharp `horn` (sharp.js; tools/creaturegen/sharp/horns.py merged the field part and its slender detail tip into one centreline): smooth, sunk in the skull, a true point. (2026-11-08, fair_bases.py) The HORNS' roots are FAIRED into the skull (sharp.js horn `fair`): a small boss, the smooth union of horn and skin, no crease. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur.",
